        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c195e9de-23d5-595f-9489-8e9879eaf189",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Hong Kong, Diamond Hill, Lantau Island, Ngong Ping\n- Organizations: Chi Lin Nunnery, Po Lin Monastery\n- Products: Tian Tan Buddha\n- Topics: Buddhist temples, tourist attractions\n\nFacts:\n- Chi Lin Nunnery is a prominent Buddhist temple in Diamond Hill, Hong Kong, and it was built in the Tang Dynasty architectural style.\n- Tian Tan Buddha is a large bronze statue of Buddha Shakyamuni in Ngong Ping on Lantau Island, Hong Kong, and it was completed in 1993.\n- Po Lin Monastery is a prominent Buddhist temple on Lantau Island, Hong Kong.\n- Po Lin Monastery and Tian Tan Buddha are both significant tourist attractions in Ngong Ping.\n- Po Lin Monastery is famous for the nearby outdoor bronze statue Tian Tan Buddha.\n- Tian Tan Buddha attracts many visitors on weekends and holidays.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "b970df8e-2821-56ac-9ac3-d363b8bbc24b",
        "text": "Page: Buddhism in Hong Kong. Sentence: Among the most prominent Buddhist temples in the city there are the Chi Lin Nunnery in Diamond Hill, built in the Tang Dynasty's architectural style; the Po Lin Monastery on Lantau Island, famous for the outdoor bronze statue, Tian Tan Buddha, which attracts a large number of visitors during the weekends and holidays.\nPage: Tian Tan Buddha. Sentence: Tian Tan Buddha, also known as the Big Buddha, is a large bronze statue of Buddha Shakyamuni, completed in 1993, and located at Ngong Ping, Lantau Island, in Hong Kong.\nPage: Ngong Ping 360. Sentence: This is home to the Po Lin Monastery and the Tian Tan Buddha, both already significant tourist attractions in their own right.",
